7. Reflection: Why Enterprise Systems React Automatically to Data Changes?
  ->Enterprise systems handle large amounts of data and users. 
  ->Automatic reactions to data changes improve efficiency, reduce manual work, ensure consistency, and provide real-time responses.
  ->Event-driven automation helps organizations respond quickly to important business events such as registrations, payments, approvals, and notifications.

Reflective Questions & Answers

1. Why do systems need triggers?
  ->Triggers allow systems to automatically perform actions when data changes occur, reducing manual effort and improving efficiency.
2. Difference between polling and event-driven systems?
  ->Polling: System continuously checks for changes.
  ->Event-Driven: System reacts immediately when an event occurs.
3. Why are database queries important?
  ->Queries help retrieve specific data quickly and efficiently from large databases.
4. When should Flows be preferred over Triggers?
  ->Flows should be preferred when the automation is simple and can be implemented without coding.
5. What problems happen if automation logic becomes too complex?
  ->Complex automation becomes difficult to maintain, debug, and understand, which can increase errors.
6. Why should developers think carefully before automating actions?
  ->Poorly designed automation can create unnecessary processes, performance issues, and incorrect business outcomes.
